  "narrative": {
    "summaryIntro": "Trimbakeshwar Temple is one of the twelve Jyotirlingas and is dedicated to Lord Shiva as Trimbakeshwar (Lord of Three-eyed Shiva). Located in Nashik, Maharashtra, at the foothills of the Brahmagiri mountain, the temple is known for its intricate Deccan architectural style. The name 'Trimbak' literally means three-eyed, referring to Shiva's three eyes.\n\nThe temple is situated near the source of the sacred Godavari River and is an important pilgrimage site in western India. The temple features elaborate stone carvings and is surrounded by ghats on the river. The site holds immense spiritual significance, particularly during Kumbh Mela celebrations in Nashik, making it one of the major pilgrimage destinations in Maharashtra.",
